      "versionNonce": 629653100,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "type": "text",
      "x": 820,
      "y": 1108,
      "width": 388.96000000000004,
      "height": 21.25,
      "text": "WRITE / INGEST PATH   (async, at-least-once)",
      "fontSize": 17,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "WRITE / INGEST PATH   (async, at-least-once)",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "el88",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 116146606,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1280285447,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "type": "text",
      "x": 820,
      "y": 1143,
      "width": 525.6,
      "height": 285.0,
      "text": "W1  POST /documents    json body  OR  multipart file\n        > 5 MB -> presigned S3 PUT, client uploads direct to S3\nW2  ONE txn:  INSERT documents (status=PENDING) + INSERT index_outbox\nW2b Raw bytes land in S3 under {tenant}/{doc_id}/raw\nW3  Reply 202 { id, status:\"PENDING\" }     everything after is async\nW4  Relay -> Kafka doc.extract.v1     key = tenant_id:doc_id\nW5  Extraction worker pulls the job, GETs the blob from S3\n        Tika -> text + per-page char offsets\n        no text layer? -> Tesseract OCR on the slow pool\n        chunk 800 tokens / 100 overlap, never split mid-sentence\nW5c     emit N chunk events -> doc.index.v1      status=EXTRACTED\nW6  Indexer bulks 500/2s -> chunks-{group} + docs-{group}\n        drops the event if incoming.version < indexed.version\nW7  status=LIVE, INCR inv:{tenant} -> tenant query cache goes void\n\nFailure   3x backoff -> DLQ + alert. Encrypted or corrupt PDF sets\n          status=FAILED + failure_reason, visible on GET /documents/{id}.\n          Never silently dropped -- a missing doc is a support ticket.\nDELETE    soft-delete in PG + tombstone -> delete_by_query(doc_id)",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "W1  POST /documents    json body  OR  multipart file\n        > 5 MB -> presigned S3 PUT, client uploads direct to S3\nW2  ONE txn:  INSERT documents (status=PENDING) + INSERT index_outbox\nW2b Raw bytes land in S3 under {tenant}/{doc_id}/raw\nW3  Reply 202 { id, status:\"PENDING\" }     everything after is async\nW4  Relay -> Kafka doc.extract.v1     key = tenant_id:doc_id\nW5  Extraction worker pulls the job, GETs the blob from S3\n        Tika -> text + per-page char offsets\n        no text layer? -> Tesseract OCR on the slow pool\n        chunk 800 tokens / 100 overlap, never split mid-sentence\nW5c     emit N chunk events -> doc.index.v1      status=EXTRACTED\nW6  Indexer bulks 500/2s -> chunks-{group} + docs-{group}\n        drops the event if incoming.version < indexed.version\nW7  status=LIVE, INCR inv:{tenant} -> tenant query cache goes void\n\nFailure   3x backoff -> DLQ + alert. Encrypted or corrupt PDF sets\n          status=FAILED + failure_reason, visible on GET /documents/{id}.\n          Never silently dropped -- a missing doc is a support ticket.\nDELETE    soft-delete in PG + tombstone -> delete_by_query(doc_id)",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "el89",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#f08c00",
      "backgroundColor": "#fff9db",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": {
        "type": 3
      },
      "seed": 390887331,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 1121481225,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 1640,
      "y": 1090,
      "width": 760,
      "height": 516.0
    },
    {
      "id": "el90",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1971c2",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1574963608,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 717440071,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1660,
      "y": 1108,
      "width": 123.76,
      "height": 21.25,
      "text": "KEY TRADE-OFFS",
      "fontSize": 17,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "KEY TRADE-OFFS",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "el91",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 1527703408,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 956887592,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1660,
      "y": 1143,
      "width": 525.6,
      "height": 435.0,
      "text": "Two-stage pipeline      extraction is slow and CPU-bound, indexing is\n                        fast and IO-bound. Separate topics and worker\n                        pools so a 300-page OCR job cannot stall a 2 KB\n                        text note queued behind it.\n\n202 + status field      write p99 stays < 30ms. Client polls\n                        GET /documents/{id} or takes a webhook. Search\n                        is eventually consistent: ~2s text, ~30s OCR.\n\nPostgres is the truth   OpenSearch is derived and disposable, S3 holds\n                        the original bytes. Lose the search cluster and\n                        you replay from S3 into a fresh index.\n\nChunk, don't index      BM25 over a whole 300-page PDF ranks badly -- a\nwhole files             two-word match scores like a dense section, and\n                        you have no usable snippet to show. Passage-level\n                        index + collapse by doc_id gives one hit per\n                        document with the best passage attached.\n\nShared index, routed    cheapest for 10M docs across many small tenants.\nby tenant_id            A whale tenant (>5M docs) is promoted to its own\n                        index via tenants.index_group, no code change.\n\nIsolation in 3 layers   JWT claim -> Postgres RLS -> mandatory ES term\n                        filter injected by the repository layer. S3 keys\n                        are tenant-prefixed with per-tenant SSE-KMS keys.\n\nCache TTL over          bounded 60s staleness beats fan-out key deletion.\ninvalidation scans      Busting a tenant = one counter increment.",
      "fontSize": 12,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Two-stage pipeline      extraction is slow and CPU-bound, indexing is\n                        fast and IO-bound. Separate topics and worker\n                        pools so a 300-page OCR job cannot stall a 2 KB\n                        text note queued behind it.\n\n202 + status field      write p99 stays < 30ms. Client polls\n                        GET /documents/{id} or takes a webhook. Search\n                        is eventually consistent: ~2s text, ~30s OCR.\n\nPostgres is the truth   OpenSearch is derived and disposable, S3 holds\n                        the original bytes. Lose the search cluster and\n                        you replay from S3 into a fresh index.\n\nChunk, don't index      BM25 over a whole 300-page PDF ranks badly -- a\nwhole files             two-word match scores like a dense section, and\n                        you have no usable snippet to show. Passage-level\n                        index + collapse by doc_id gives one hit per\n                        document with the best passage attached.\n\nShared index, routed    cheapest for 10M docs across many small tenants.\nby tenant_id            A whale tenant (>5M docs) is promoted to its own\n                        index via tenants.index_group, no code change.\n\nIsolation in 3 layers   JWT claim -> Postgres RLS -> mandatory ES term\n                        filter injected by the repository layer. S3 keys\n                        are tenant-prefixed with per-tenant SSE-KMS keys.\n\nCache TTL over          bounded 60s staleness beats fan-out key deletion.\ninvalidation scans      Busting a tenant = one counter increment.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "el92",
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#868e96",
      "backgroundColor": "#f8f9fa",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 2,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
